  "reasoning": "The patient's primary symptoms are swelling in the legs, difficulty fitting into shoes due to the swelling, and discomfort when sitting for extended periods. These clinical features strongly point toward venous insufficiency or varicose veins, which frequently present with lower extremity edema and aching/discomfort. Other listed conditions do not align with the symptom profile: diabetes would typically include excessive thirst and frequent urination; hypertension would present with headaches, dizziness, or chest discomfort; arthritis involves joint pain and stiffness; and infections like malaria, dengue, or typhoid would feature systemic signs like high fever, chills, or severe body aches. Since leg swelling and associated discomfort are the hallmark complaints here without supporting evidence for the alternatives, varicose veins is the established diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
